  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.Bala Krishna vs State Of Ap on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5058 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.66 of 2019 of Ongole I Town Police Station, Prakasam District, which was registered against him for the offences under Sections 188, 273, 420 of IPC and Secs.58, 59, 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 07.03.2019 at 21:30 hours, the complainant along with staff, on credible information proceeded to the house of petitioner situated at Harerama Bazar, Lawyerpeta, Ongole, seized the banned tobacco products from the possession of petitioner under a cover of panchanama, later he arrested him and registered a case in Crime No.66 of 2019 for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
